<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2012/Flash-5.jpg" alt="Starting a conformation portrait of a chestnut horse " width="600" height="417" /></p>
<p>I've laid down most of the body in one long painting session. &nbsp;Actually a morning and afternoon in the studio with lunch and a nap in between. &nbsp;I paint much better when I'm rested.</p>
<p>Some of the half-tone areas will need more work, but by getting everything down at once I've kept some of the painting-from-life feel that I set out to achieve.</p>
<p>I found a couple of drawing mistakes while working on the body (chest outline and position of the blaze) and I was able to correct them fairly easily.</p>